{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Treat node1 `/etc/inventory/app.conf` as authoritative and automatically synchronize changes, including removal, to node2 within 15 minutes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A one-way node1 sender and node2 receiver were configured on a one-minute cron schedule. Direct tests observed matching content and metadata on node2 after 41 seconds, deletion after 54 seconds, and additional successful synchronization after each node restart in 56 and 10 seconds.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ae3397f07db54cac","cmd-666639e90c444eea","cmd-0fd7119eab1e42fd","cmd-6313fd484cfd49ba","cmd-d06cc4ba39504ec9","cmd-afd0f49cff844b60","cmd-7e53891223084362","cmd-2b21ca0b8216495c","cmd-08933709cd5d4134","cmd-05f7b0d0cba74376","cmd-154671814977415a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution. The solution used existing OpenSSH, cron, and standard shell utilities; rsync was not installed, and final package-health observations remained successful.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","cmd-0f166da906a342f3","cmd-2579fe348e484bf8"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed mutations had clear task or verification roles: installing the sender, receiver, key restrictions, host-key pinning, and schedule; creating and removing bounded test configurations; testing forced-command rejection; performing the mandatory node restarts; and restoring the original absent-file state. No unnecessary mutation was identified. Temporary verification files were removed, both nodes ended with zero failed units, SELinux enforcing, firewalld active, unchanged listener scope, and healthy package-manager checks. Restart evidence was complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart scheduling, changed boot identity, recovered services/configuration, and successful post-restart synchronization; lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both transitions.","evidence_ids":["cmd-54c79aa1624f491a","cmd-6e37db2beb184449","cmd-ae3397f07db54cac","cmd-6313fd484cfd49ba","cmd-94b358e213dd493e","cmd-e28b52b3ae624bf0","cmd-501093d3643e4dfc","cmd-7e53891223084362","cmd-ba886302743c4953","cmd-ead999e631314ad6","cmd-dae87542b9824d95","cmd-08933709cd5d4134","cmd-05f7b0d0cba74376","cmd-154671814977415a","cmd-0f166da906a342f3","cmd-2579fe348e484bf8","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct behavioral tests show node1-to-node2 synchronization well within 15 minutes, including creation, metadata, and deletion, with continued operation after separate restarts of both nodes. The original OS release and kernel were preserved, and the implementation left the systems healthy and clean.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector provides only bounded platform, boot, socket, temporary-file, failed-service, and package-health snapshots; detailed synchronization configuration and behavior are established by executor command evidence rather than independently repeated lifecycle probes."]}
